We’re consolidating everything into one Pantheon architecture: PRISM — the Universal Representation & Reconstruction Compiler.

Its job is to take almost anything—an image, SVG, language, music, motion, code, or a conceptual model—recover its underlying structure, and reconstruct it in another medium using inference, common sense, and feedback.

The key addition is that the compiler doesn’t just translate. It can hypothesize missing information, test its reconstruction, repair errors, and learn reusable generative rules.

It unifies Semantic Alpha, Semantic PCA, Abductive Reversibility, the Prism Guitar, Painter’s Atelier, Delta Calculus, and your existing Pantheon machinery.

