# 22. MINIMUM VIABLE REFERENCE TESTS
TEST A — ALPHA PRESERVATION
Input:
PNG with opaque, semitransparent,
and fully transparent regions.
Requirement:
Preserve meaningful alpha behavior during
supported raster/vector conversions.
TEST B — INVARIANT PRESERVATION
Input:
Simple logo with known component relationships.
Requirement:
SVG reconstruction retains selected shape,
topology, and identity constraints.
TEST C — AMBIGUOUS INPUT
Input:
Partially obscured object.
Requirement:
Retain multiple hypotheses and distinguish
observed from inferred geometry.
TEST D — SEMANTIC TRANSLATION
Input:
Sentence describing an organizational hierarchy.
Requirement:
Construct diagram and reverse description
without losing declared relationships.
TEST E — CROSS-MODAL STRUCTURE
Input:
Patterned visual sequence.
Requirement:
Generate musical structure preserving chosen
repetition and contrast relationships.
TEST F — FAILURE DETECTION
Input:
Candidate translation with a deliberately
incorrect invariant.
Requirement:
Detect discrepancy, classify error,
and attempt appropriate repair.
TEST G — EXACT VERSUS INFERRED
Input:
Lossy source transformation.
Requirement:
Demonstrate exact recovery only when source
or sufficient residual information exists;
otherwise report reconstruction status.
